lantic Ocean but it's not just  tourists and hotels chainsaw  manufacturers steel also managed to find  the theoretical know-how to complement  the practical training will attends the  local community college four days a week  the classes he takes fit his training  program and they provide him with  theoretical background like courses in  engineering dynamics gross is the only  one in his class who was part of the  steel program most of the students here  study only Theory wills daily schedule  as a trainee is demanding but he's  holding up well he used to be a  production line worker at steel and he  says this is much better  well since I'd been trying to study  towards that field of degree I kind of  knew I was going to be getting into some  involvement but not this not this level  of complication it is really different  for me yeah I am yeah so it definitely  pays off for the trainees but what about  the company itself manager Simon dance  often drops by the production line he's  trying to improve employee development  and he wants feedback from his employees  the u.s. makes up Steel's most important  market outside Europe the tools produced  here generate an annual turnover of 716  million euros steel products are  relatively high priced but Nantz knows  that only good quality will keep  attracting buyers he's convinced the  training program is a key factor it's  it's an investment in employees skills  and when we can invest long-term in  employees not six months down the road  but six years down the road it's gonna  make a difference in the product and  it's going to make a difference for the  customer  the chainsaw is made here in Virginia  Beach don't carry the made in Germany  label but future skilled workers like  will grouse will make sure that these  tools will work just as well as the ones  that are made in Germany  [Music]

